/-!
# Height four at `k = 4`: the compensation certificate, concrete part

Codex's (OpenAI) endpoint compensation (`ai_research_notes/cx/h4k4/NOTE.md`), in the reduced form
of `ai_research_notes/H4_K4_REVIEW_2026-10-26.md` Part 1(d): in an endpoint fibre the alternative
term differs from the bad one only in the endpoint list, `Y'ᵣ = (Yᵣ + p) − q` with `p ∉ Yᵣ` the
erased colour and `q ≠ p`. On the colours `C = {0, 1, 2}`, `a = 3`, `b = 4` and a fresh colour `5`:

* forward edge families (`YF i`, next column `BF`): the first list `i` (`C−z+a`, `C−x+a`, `C−y+a`,
  `C+a`), `p ∈ {z, a, fresh}` (`pcF`), `q ∈ {x, y, b}` or no erasure (`qcF`, `6` is never present);
* the central family (`YM`, `BM`): `p ∈ {a, b, fresh}` (`pcM`), `q ∈ {x, y, z}` or none (`qcM`).

Each of the `5` bad seam vectors and `60` alternatives is evaluated by the kernel (`decide`), and
the `60` paired sums are nonnegative at the twelve rays of `K` (`certF`, `certM`). The smallest
paired slack, normalised by `w_A = 1`, is `61/500` (E2), as in Codex's table. Generated by
`ai_research_notes/h4k4lean/gencomp.py`.
-/

